<%#
  Per-modal card WIDTH registry — the engine modal host's first extension point
  (studio-engine 0.65.0, window.StudioModals.CARD_WIDTHS).

  The host's card is max-w-sm by default, which is right for a question and two
  buttons. A modal carrying something with an INTRINSIC aspect ratio needs more:
  wallet-setup shows a 16:9 explainer video, and at max-w-sm the player is small
  enough that the thing it is teaching cannot be read.

  KEYED BY MODAL ID, NOT PASSED AS A PROP, and that is the whole reason this is a
  registry. wallet-setup is opened from three places (the board's entry gate, the
  onboarding chain driver, and the post-Connect reopen); a prop would have to be
  remembered at each, and one miss renders the same card at two different widths
  depending on how the user arrived.

  WHY A PARTIAL AND NOT AN IMPORTMAP MODULE. The engine host resolves the width
  in cardClasses() and merges this map at the top of its own inline script, so
  the registration has to be on window before that script runs. A synchronous
  inline script runs during HTML parse; importmap modules are deferred and load
  after Alpine has already started. Same reason shared/_alpine_factories and
  studio/_birthday_assets are inlined at layout level rather than shipped as
  modules.

  RENDER IT ABOVE the host in EVERY layout that mounts the host. This app has two
  (layouts/application and layouts/modal_preview); a layout that renders the host
  without this one silently falls back to max-w-sm for every id, which looks like
  a styling regression rather than a missing include.

  Merged rather than assigned so the map survives another registration and a
  future engine default. Add a width: one line below, plus nothing else.
%>
<script>
  window.StudioModals = window.StudioModals || {};
  window.StudioModals.CARD_WIDTHS = Object.assign({}, window.StudioModals.CARD_WIDTHS || {}, {
    'wallet-setup': 'max-w-md'
  });
</script>
